1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,393
‪EPISODE 3

3
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,798
‪How dare you blackmail me?

4
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:57,635
‪I didn't make a fuss
‪when you copied my designs last season.

5
00:02:57,719 --> 00:03:00,221
‪But I didn't think you'd copy
‪my <i>‪haenyeo</i>‪ diver dress.

6
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:04,392
‪It was a special dress I made
‪while thinking of my grandmother.

7
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:06,811
‪Hey, listen.

8
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:10,440
‪Why would I copy the design
‪of a lowly nobody like you?

9
00:03:10,523 --> 00:03:12,775
‪You can run your mouth all you want,

10
00:03:12,859 --> 00:03:14,444
‪but who would believe you?

11
00:03:16,321 --> 00:03:18,698
‪Wait and find out if they believe me.

12
00:03:19,282 --> 00:03:21,784
‪Circumstantial evidence
‪that you copied my designs

13
00:03:22,493 --> 00:03:24,621
‪was caught on the surveillance cameras.

14
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:34,380
‪You came well-prepared, didn't you?

15
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:37,133
‪Give me that phone.

16
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:42,472
‪Put my name on the design.

17
00:03:42,555 --> 00:03:44,140
‪Give me the phone!

18
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:47,143
‪-Say you used my designs!
‪-Give me the damn phone!

19
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:10,416
<i>‪Da-mi!</i>

20
00:06:00,651 --> 00:06:01,819
‪Don't you have something to say?

21
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,074
‪What do you mean?

22
00:06:07,158 --> 00:06:08,451
‪It wasn't a coincidence, was it?

23
00:06:10,578 --> 00:06:12,580
‪The mountain where we first met,

24
00:06:12,663 --> 00:06:15,917
‪the taxi driver's body in the trunk,
‪and now, Jang Eun-ju.

25
00:06:17,001 --> 00:06:19,587
‪It's a huge stretch,
‪but let's say that was all a coincidence.

26
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,130
‪But for this to be by chance too?

27
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:26,010
‪What is it you want to say?

28
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,428
‪If it were you…

29
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,561
‪Let's talk about it another time.

30
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,231
‪You should go inside and warm up.

31
00:06:44,904 --> 00:06:45,822
‪About earlier…

32
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:51,285
‪Thank you.

33
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:57,250
‪I might be used to how things are,

34
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:00,670
‪but that doesn't mean I'm not afraid.

35
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:08,928
‪Please take care of this for me.

36
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:13,558
‪You'd be better at handling it than me.

37
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:35,580
‪I swear, it was a setup.

38
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:37,331
‪There must be a mistake!

39
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:40,877
‪-Don't take any photos.
‪-It's all just a misunderstanding!

40
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,962
‪-Don't take photos.
‪-Ms. Kim!

41
00:07:43,045 --> 00:07:44,213
‪-Ms. Jung!
‪-Can you prove it was…

42
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:45,673
‪-Ms. Kim.
‪-Yes?

43
00:07:45,756 --> 00:07:47,550
‪Find out whoever did this.

44
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:49,302
‪-I'll demand reparation.
‪-Yes, ma'am.

45
00:07:49,385 --> 00:07:50,386
‪Be gentle with her.

46
00:07:58,769 --> 00:08:00,813
‪Come on out. Watch your step.

47
00:08:01,856 --> 00:08:04,859
‪-Thank you. Please watch your step.
‪-Grandma?

48
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,570
‪This is where you'll be staying.

49
00:08:07,653 --> 00:08:11,616
‪You'll rest in the lobby for a while,
‪and then we'll hand out the keys.

50
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:13,493
‪We'll show you where to go then.

51
00:08:14,869 --> 00:08:16,579
‪-Shall we?
‪-Hey.

52
00:08:16,662 --> 00:08:17,872
‪Grandma, are you in Jeju Island?

53
00:08:17,955 --> 00:08:21,000
<i>‪Why would I be there? I'm at the temple.</i>

54
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,793
<i>‪-Are you in Jeju Island?</i>
‪-Yeah.

55
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:25,171
‪Are you sure you're not here?

56
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:27,298
<i>‪What nonsense are you on about?</i>

57
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:31,260
<i>‪By the way, you must stay away</i>
<i>‪from large bodies of water today.</i>

58
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:32,220
‪Okay.

59
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:38,017
‪Man, is she psychic or something?

60
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,438
‪Did you reach the airport safely?

61
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:44,607
<i>‪Yeah, I'm almost there.</i>

62
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:46,776
‪You didn't have to send a car.

63
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:48,152
<i>‪I heard about the unfortunate accident.</i>

64
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,155
‪I'll let you buy me a meal
‪if you're that grateful.

65
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:54,450
<i>‪Sure.</i>

66
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:56,994
‪I'll be going to Seoul soon,
‪so don't forget.

67
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:08,756
‪Why are you doing that yourself
‪when we have gardeners?

68
00:09:11,592 --> 00:09:12,593
‪I heard about the nuisance.

69
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:14,679
‪Oh, it's been taken care of.

70
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:18,891
‪By the way,
‪did you have a visitor earlier?

71
00:09:24,855 --> 00:09:26,482
‪They grow so quickly.

72
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:30,945
‪If you don't pluck them in time,
‪the weeds will take over the whole garden.

73
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,410
<i>‪Hey.</i>

74
00:09:37,493 --> 00:09:40,913
‪You should stay with her
‪until Da-mi is moved to the burial site.

75
00:09:42,623 --> 00:09:46,294
‪We can't both miss work,
‪so I had to come back.

76
00:09:49,422 --> 00:09:50,965
‪But it just breaks my heart.

77
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:52,550
‪Okay, bye.

78
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:14,363
‪I was definitely within arm's reach,

79
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:18,451
‪but I get the feeling
‪she deliberately avoided grabbing me.

80
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:21,621
‪About earlier… Thank you.

81
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:24,624
‪I might be used to how things are,

82
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:27,418
‪but that doesn't mean I'm not afraid.

83
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,297
‪What was she thanking me for?

84
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:34,050
‪She's a strange one.

85
00:10:56,906 --> 00:10:58,658
‪I heard you rejected Min-hwan's offer.

86
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,534
‪Yes.

87
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:04,330
‪I'll flesh out the strategy
‪I showed you last time.

88
00:11:04,413 --> 00:11:06,707
‪Review it for me again.
‪I'm confident I can manage.

89
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:09,126
‪How did it feel to see him again?

90
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:10,211
‪Well…

91
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:15,800
‪Did you send me to Jeju Island
‪because of Min-hwan?

92
00:11:15,883 --> 00:11:18,219
‪Yes, and since we're on the topic…

93
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:20,721
‪I quite like him. What about you?

94
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:24,308
‪You mean, romantically?

95
00:11:25,059 --> 00:11:27,645
‪He's just a friend I went to school with.

96
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:29,397
‪I told you last time, didn't I?

97
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:32,441
‪To squash the rumor
‪that's going on about you,

98
00:11:33,275 --> 00:11:34,902
‪marriage is the best option.

99
00:11:34,985 --> 00:11:36,821
‪-Grandma.
‪-We can't have such rumors.

100
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:40,491
‪It's not just about the hotel.
‪What about our family's reputation?

101
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:43,536
‪Dispel the rumor yourself,
‪with a marriage.

102
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:46,789
‪Come on, this isn't the Joseon Dynasty.

103
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:49,917
‪You can't force me to get married.

104
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,043
‪Your marriage

105
00:11:52,294 --> 00:11:53,671
‪isn't just any union.

106
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:57,425
‪What if the line of succession
‪passes to Dong-jun and Ha-ri?

107
00:11:58,342 --> 00:12:01,804
‪There is the disadvantage
‪that their father isn't my biological son,

108
00:12:01,887 --> 00:12:03,139
‪but you know that

109
00:12:03,222 --> 00:12:06,183
‪when it comes to succession,
‪it's not just about blood.

110
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:10,646
‪With Min-hwan's help,
‪you could sign with a foreign hotel chain,

111
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:12,815
‪and naturally get together in the process…

112
00:12:12,898 --> 00:12:14,483
‪I have no intention of doing that.

113
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:15,568
‪And I

114
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:17,445
‪don't plan to wait for long.

115
00:12:18,654 --> 00:12:19,864
‪This is the right time

116
00:12:19,947 --> 00:12:23,576
‪to clear up the rumors
‪that are going around about you.

117
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:25,536
‪Get married within two months.

118
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:27,413
‪If you don't,

119
00:12:27,496 --> 00:12:30,082
‪I'll bring the Reina licensing talk
‪back to the table.

120
00:12:30,916 --> 00:12:32,126
‪And Siena Hall too.

121
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,840
‪Well, at least

122
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,758
‪make it an engagement for now.

123
00:12:39,842 --> 00:12:41,886
‪Since it was my engagement ceremony
‪that fell through.

124
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:44,180
‪The deadline remains the same. Two months.

125
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:48,184
‪On that note, I'd be happy with Min-hwan.

126
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:51,896
‪But like you said,
‪this isn't the Joseon Dynasty.

127
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:59,069
‪Still, he should at least
‪measure up to our family.

128
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:01,697
‪Okay. Let's get back to it.

129
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,257
‪Go on ahead.

130
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:27,890
‪Now, you're putting Seung-jae behind you

131
00:13:27,973 --> 00:13:29,725
‪and getting out there
‪on blind dates, okay?

132
00:13:35,105 --> 00:13:37,399
‪We bought everything you wanted.

133
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:41,070
‪Okay.

134
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:45,407
‪Does Grandma have no interest
‪in opening a department store?

135
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:46,492
‪Reina Department Store.

136
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:49,036
‪I'm sure I'd do a good job running it.

137
00:13:50,204 --> 00:13:52,790
‪It's hard enough to get her
‪to give us another art gallery.

138
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:54,917
‪Forget about a department store.

139
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,670
‪Yeo-ri hasn't caught on yet, right?

140
00:13:58,170 --> 00:13:59,213
‪About the hotel artworks.

141
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:02,800
‪Cheon Ha-ri?

142
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:05,928
‪Is that you, Min-hwan?

143
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,513
‪Wow, how long has it been?

144
00:14:07,596 --> 00:14:10,891
‪Oh, my goodness. Look who it is.

145
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:12,059
‪How have you been?

146
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:13,435
‪I've been very well.

147
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:14,687
‪When did you come back to Korea?

148
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:17,022
‪Well, not too long ago.

149
00:14:17,606 --> 00:14:19,567
‪We haven't met in a while.
‪How about we eat together?

150
00:14:22,695 --> 00:14:24,905
‪I'm here to buy a gift, so I can't today.

151
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:26,740
‪I'll treat you to something nice soon.

152
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:28,409
‪You too, Ms. Ok.

153
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:37,501
‪Come in.

154
00:14:41,505 --> 00:14:42,423
‪Chairwoman Baek.

155
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:43,424
‪Min-hwan.

156
00:14:47,219 --> 00:14:48,554
‪It's been so long.

157
00:14:50,848 --> 00:14:52,182
‪Min-hwan.

158
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:54,393
‪-This is for you.
‪-Goodness.

159
00:14:54,894 --> 00:14:56,145
‪Oh, gosh.

160
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:57,646
‪It's beautiful.

161
00:14:58,647 --> 00:15:00,691
‪You didn't have to get me anything.

162
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:03,736
‪It's so nice to see you in person
‪after just some phone calls.

163
00:15:03,819 --> 00:15:05,529
‪-It really is.
‪-Let's sit down.

164
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:10,200
‪You haven't changed at all.
‪You look even more radiant.

165
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,161
‪Oh, don't you tease an old woman.

166
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:18,918
‪I heard you and Yeo-ri
‪didn't reach an agreement.

167
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:22,212
‪You sent her over knowing
‪how it would turn out.

168
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:24,715
‪I appreciate the cooperation.

169
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:27,009
‪Goodness.

170
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,094
‪Should we have dinner with Yeo-ri?

171
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,263
‪I'd love to.

172
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,140
‪What was it that you liked to eat?

173
00:15:34,099 --> 00:15:35,392
‪Anything you like?

174
00:15:37,978 --> 00:15:39,438
‪I don't really mind it much.

175
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,190
‪Hello, ma'am.

176
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,192
‪Ms. Cheon's in, right?

177
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:46,236
‪She just left to go home.

178
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,696
‪Should I give her a call?

179
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,281
‪No need.

180
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:51,283
‪She doesn't even take my calls after work.

181
00:15:52,743 --> 00:15:54,286
‪I've spoiled her.

182
00:15:55,704 --> 00:15:56,580
‪That's too bad.

183
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:59,959
‪We'll have to eat together
‪some other time.

184
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:02,252
‪No. I like this even better.

185
00:16:02,336 --> 00:16:03,545
‪We can spend some quality time.

186
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:04,713
‪Right?

187
00:16:04,797 --> 00:16:06,674
‪Let's just relax and eat something nice.

188
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:07,591
‪Sounds good.

189
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:32,658
<i>‪Min-hwan and Ji-hwan aren't twins?</i>

190
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:34,994
‪Keep your voice down.

191
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:36,620
‪My sister will kill me if she hears you.

192
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:42,209
‪The truth is, after my sister
‪learned she was infertile,

193
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,962
‪she adopted a baby from the US.

194
00:16:45,462 --> 00:16:47,631
‪But right before she returned to Korea,

195
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:49,842
‪-she miraculously got pregnant.
‪-Oh, gosh.

196
00:16:49,925 --> 00:16:51,885
‪That's why she delayed her return

197
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:54,304
‪and came back
‪after giving birth to Ji-hwan.

198
00:16:54,847 --> 00:16:56,390
‪I wondered why she stayed abroad so long.

199
00:16:56,473 --> 00:16:59,685
‪So Min-hwan was adopted, after all.

200
00:16:59,768 --> 00:17:01,854
‪-Exactly.
‪-No wonder…

201
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:18,620
‪Could that be why they want to
‪send Min-hwan abroad to study?

202
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,332
‪What are you doing over there?

203
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:24,293
‪Yeo-ri, you're here too.

204
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:26,628
‪-Join us for some fruit.
‪-No, thank you.

205
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:29,339
‪We were on our way out.

206
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:30,340
‪Were you?

207
00:17:32,176 --> 00:17:33,052
‪Let's go.

208
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:44,980
‪What do you want?

209
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,899
‪We agreed to a bet.

210
00:17:48,567 --> 00:17:49,485
‪Can't it wait?

211
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:52,988
‪No way. A promise is a promise.

212
00:17:53,697 --> 00:17:55,074
‪Keep your word.

213
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:05,876
‪If I win,

214
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:08,629
‪give me the game console
‪you bought yesterday.

215
00:18:12,966 --> 00:18:14,885
‪That's not fair. It's mine.

216
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:16,970
‪Then beat me.

217
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:02,558
‪Hey, Gang-uk!

218
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:04,184
‪-I think I forgot something.
‪-Gang-uk.

219
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:05,727
‪-What?
‪-I got the office next to yours.

220
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,187
‪Then we're just neighbors.

221
00:19:07,271 --> 00:19:08,730
‪We have a connection, don't we?

222
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:10,691
‪-Will you please…
‪-Here.

223
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:12,359
‪Thank you.

224
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:14,528
‪How long has it been?

225
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:16,905
‪What do you mean?
‪We met at Do-jun's wedding.

226
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:19,116
‪That's a really long time for us.

227
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:21,869
‪-Jeez, you still yap too much.
‪-Isn't that Prosecutor Im Seo-hyeon

228
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:23,787
‪from the Ministry of Justice's
‪Criminal Affairs Division?

229
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,497
‪What's going on? Do they know each other?

230
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:27,082
‪They don't just know each other.

231
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:30,544
‪What do you mean? Did they date?

232
00:19:30,627 --> 00:19:32,963
‪I wouldn't say they dated.

233
00:19:33,046 --> 00:19:35,549
‪Ever since
‪they went to the same university,

234
00:19:35,632 --> 00:19:39,219
‪their relationship has been like
‪that of the Earth and the moon.

235
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:40,262
‪The Earth and the moon?

236
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:44,099
‪-Earth's gravity pulls the moon, right?
‪-Right.

237
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:48,937
‪Im pulls Ma close with all her might,

238
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:53,984
‪but Ma spins around her
‪without ever getting too close.

239
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:56,111
‪It's quite strange.

240
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:59,198
‪Whenever Ma is
‪transferred somewhere for work,

241
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:01,783
‪Im also gets herself transferred there.

242
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:05,746
‪And when Ma transfers somewhere else,
‪Im follows him there too.

243
00:20:06,330 --> 00:20:08,624
‪Does she have connections
‪with the higher-ups?

244
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:09,958
‪That's what I don't get.

245
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:12,711
‪It's fascinating.

246
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:14,087
‪The Earth and the moon…

247
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:17,591
‪Yes?

248
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:20,427
‪Hello.

249
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:22,304
‪It's Mr. Kang, the CEO.

250
00:20:23,263 --> 00:20:25,265
‪-Welcome.
‪-Thank you.

251
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:28,352
‪I didn't expect to get a call from you.

252
00:20:28,435 --> 00:20:31,939
‪I felt bad that we didn't get to talk
‪after meeting at the department store.

253
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:33,815
‪It's been so long since we met,

254
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:36,568
‪and I wanted to treat you to a meal.

255
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,278
‪Was the drive here all right?

256
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,656
‪-Yes, it was fine.
‪-Was it?

257
00:20:42,824 --> 00:20:45,118
‪The thing is, I heard somewhere

258
00:20:45,202 --> 00:20:50,207
‪that G1A Group is trying to sell
‪Fiel Seoul to another company.

259
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:51,667
‪CL Group has decided to join

260
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:54,127
‪the bidding war to acquire it, right?

261
00:20:54,211 --> 00:20:57,297
‪Well, we haven't
‪made our position official yet.

262
00:20:58,006 --> 00:20:59,716
‪Your sources are pretty quick.

263
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:04,137
‪They say some things are open secrets,

264
00:21:04,221 --> 00:21:07,182
‪but to be honest,
‪those in the business know everything.

265
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:10,018
‪Anyway, I heard you spearheaded

266
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,521
‪the Fiel Seoul acquisition.

267
00:21:12,604 --> 00:21:13,897
‪Well, yes.

268
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:16,441
‪If you manage to buy Fiel Seoul,

269
00:21:16,525 --> 00:21:19,027
‪will that cement your position
‪as the successor?

270
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:23,073
‪I'm so impressed, Mr. Kang.

271
00:21:24,866 --> 00:21:26,994
‪So why did you want to see me today?

272
00:21:27,077 --> 00:21:28,912
‪Oh, well…

273
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:30,122
‪From what I heard,

274
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:33,834
‪you'll need a great sum of money
‪to win the bid.

275
00:21:33,917 --> 00:21:35,627
‪Do you have the necessary funds?

276
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:39,631
‪I'm aware that they have a massive debt.

277
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:42,467
‪If you happen to be
‪in need of more funds,

278
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:45,262
‪our Reina Resort could offer

279
00:21:45,345 --> 00:21:47,556
‪a partial investment in your project.

280
00:21:49,599 --> 00:21:52,269
‪I appreciate it,
‪but we have our own financial company.

281
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:53,937
‪Not to mention that this acquisition

282
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:58,317
‪was my father's long-held ambition,
‪so I have his full support.

283
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:00,694
‪Oh, yes. I'm sure you do.

284
00:22:00,777 --> 00:22:04,114
‪Right, Chairman Kang
‪and his long-held ambition.

285
00:22:04,197 --> 00:22:07,492
‪Let's work together
‪on another project some other time.

286
00:22:08,076 --> 00:22:09,036
‪Sure.

287
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:11,413
‪Yes, I would love that.

288
00:22:13,749 --> 00:22:15,709
‪Gosh, my silly daughter Ha-ri.

289
00:22:16,335 --> 00:22:19,921
‪She never stopped talking about you,

290
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:23,425
‪but I can't reach her today
‪and I don't know where she went.

291
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:28,680
‪Hey, Ha-ri.

292
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,058
‪Take a seat.

293
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:38,356
‪This is the last time I'm visiting
‪out of loyalty as your ex.

294
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:41,485
‪Ha-ri, I think
‪I'll be out of here pretty soon.

295
00:22:41,568 --> 00:22:43,111
‪That's impossible.

296
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:44,946
‪You can't get out
‪when they found her body.

297
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:47,074
‪It's just not official yet.

298
00:22:47,949 --> 00:22:50,410
‪Let's patch things up when I get out.

299
00:22:50,494 --> 00:22:51,912
‪Patch what up?

300
00:22:51,995 --> 00:22:55,373
‪You ruined our company's
‪entire reputation.

301
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:59,795
‪Ha-ri, nothing's easier to manipulate
‪than public opinion.

302
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:01,797
‪My dad's already working on it.

303
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:04,007
‪That woman was a gold-digger
‪with a dirty past.

304
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:06,051
‪She used me from start to finish.

305
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,931
‪I believe you.

306
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:12,849
‪But my mom's turned her back on you.

307
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:16,686
‪The engagement's off,
‪and I'm supposed to cut you off.

308
00:23:18,396 --> 00:23:19,231
‪Ha-ri.

309
00:23:19,731 --> 00:23:22,734
‪The heart follows where the money is.

310
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:25,946
‪My dad's still going strong.
‪He has all the power I need.

311
00:23:28,406 --> 00:23:29,866
‪As soon as I get out,

312
00:23:30,492 --> 00:23:31,785
‪I swear on my life

313
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:34,579
‪that I'll help you take over Reina.

314
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,850
‪Why? What do you want?

315
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,060
‪I just can't seem to make sense of it.

316
00:23:58,687 --> 00:24:00,564
‪How did you know where to go?

317
00:24:01,148 --> 00:24:04,442
‪You just happened to be there
‪and found a body in the water tank,

318
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:06,486
‪and the prosecutor showed up too?

319
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:11,491
‪About the weird rumors
‪going around about you…

320
00:24:15,036 --> 00:24:17,122
‪Do you still see ghosts or something?

321
00:24:21,459 --> 00:24:22,419
‪You do, don't you?

322
00:24:24,921 --> 00:24:26,548
‪You always go

323
00:24:27,757 --> 00:24:29,593
‪a bit too far.

324
00:24:29,676 --> 00:24:32,721
‪I can't let a possessed shaman
‪take over Reina.

325
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:35,223
‪If I reveal the truth about that,

326
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:38,185
‪Grandma will give up the idea
‪of letting you take over.

327
00:24:40,645 --> 00:24:42,272
‪If that's all you have to say,
‪I'm leaving.

328
00:25:21,561 --> 00:25:24,856
‪You that inhabit the body of this woman!

329
00:25:25,523 --> 00:25:27,651
‪You evil spirit!

330
00:25:28,443 --> 00:25:30,362
‪Begone!

331
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:35,659
‪Yeo-ri?

332
00:25:37,827 --> 00:25:38,662
‪Yeo-ri.

333
00:25:41,748 --> 00:25:43,083
‪Grandma.

334
00:25:43,166 --> 00:25:44,542
‪Well done.

335
00:25:45,585 --> 00:25:46,920
‪You held up well.

336
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:51,424
‪Shaman Baek said he suppressed the evil.

337
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:52,509
‪How do you feel?

338
00:25:54,135 --> 00:25:56,388
‪Do you still see things?

339
00:26:06,564 --> 00:26:07,524
‪I don't…

340
00:26:10,568 --> 00:26:12,028
‪anymore.

341
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:16,700
‪I guess they're gone.

342
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:49,399
<i>‪Do it again.</i>

343
00:26:49,482 --> 00:26:51,318
<i>‪-Again?</i>
<i>‪-Do it again.</i>

344
00:26:57,907 --> 00:26:59,784
‪A hotel is not a facility!

345
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:01,995
‪-It's where memories are made.
‪-It's where memories are made.

346
00:27:02,078 --> 00:27:04,581
‪-Let's go, Reina!
‪-Let's go!

347
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:07,459
‪-Enjoy yourselves, everyone.
‪-Let's drink.

348
00:27:42,994 --> 00:27:45,246
‪You want me to step down
‪when I indicted him?

349
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:46,373
‪That makes no sense.

350
00:27:46,456 --> 00:27:49,918
‪Didn't I tell you to give in
‪when you had the chance?

351
00:27:50,001 --> 00:27:52,587
‪Even so. You should've shielded me.

352
00:27:53,463 --> 00:27:54,756
‪Don't you know how we work?

353
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:57,384
‪We do whatever the higher-ups tell us.

354
00:27:57,467 --> 00:27:59,969
‪What if I were to get caught
‪in the backlash?

355
00:28:00,053 --> 00:28:02,263
‪I must survive if I'm to help you out.

356
00:28:04,349 --> 00:28:06,101
‪I have to say, Assemblyman Park

357
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:07,894
‪has still got some fight left in him.

358
00:28:09,312 --> 00:28:12,023
‪Even after what his son did,
‪he managed to fight back hard.

359
00:28:13,441 --> 00:28:15,318
‪TRANSFER NOTICE
‪CRIMINAL PROSECUTION 12, MA GANG-UK

360
00:28:15,402 --> 00:28:17,112
‪PROSECUTOR MA GANG-UK TO COLD CASE UNIT

361
00:28:17,195 --> 00:28:20,657
‪We had already decided to beef up
‪Criminal Prosecution

362
00:28:21,282 --> 00:28:24,202
‪and revamp the Cold Case Unit anyway.

363
00:28:24,994 --> 00:28:27,205
‪Solve some cases while you're over there.

364
00:28:29,582 --> 00:28:30,500
‪I'll bring you back
‪when the time is right.

365
00:28:39,509 --> 00:28:42,011
‪Don't you think things are going backward?

366
00:28:42,095 --> 00:28:44,055
‪Why am I getting demoted
‪for solving a case?

367
00:28:44,139 --> 00:28:46,891
‪Accept it and go with the flow.
‪It's not like this is anything new.

368
00:28:46,975 --> 00:28:49,477
‪Fine. You wait and see.

369
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:51,521
‪Let's see what you say
‪if this happens to you.

370
00:28:51,604 --> 00:28:54,816
‪Just go, "Oh, I guess this is it then."

371
00:28:54,899 --> 00:28:56,985
‪"This is just how things are."

372
00:28:57,068 --> 00:29:00,280
‪If you take everything to heart,
‪you'll end up dying young.

373
00:29:00,363 --> 00:29:02,031
‪-Aren't I right?
‪-You are.

374
00:29:02,532 --> 00:29:04,743
‪I'm not even surprised, you know.

375
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:07,120
‪Why are you more immature
‪than your junior?

376
00:29:07,203 --> 00:29:10,081
‪Why do you keep yawning?
‪Did you not sleep well?

377
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:11,750
‪It's not that.

378
00:29:12,333 --> 00:29:15,920
‪I just had a really stressful dream
‪that felt so real.

379
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:17,380
‪In the dream,

380
00:29:18,631 --> 00:29:22,927
‪I was going somewhere when something
‪suddenly appeared in front of me.

381
00:29:23,553 --> 00:29:24,804
‪It was my late grandmother.

382
00:29:24,888 --> 00:29:27,098
‪-Okay.
‪-I asked her what was up.

383
00:29:27,182 --> 00:29:29,476
‪She just stared at me,
‪then all of a sudden

384
00:29:29,559 --> 00:29:30,894
‪she went and…

385
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:35,356
‪She hit me. She actually punched me.

386
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:37,400
‪"You good-for-nothing brat,

387
00:29:37,484 --> 00:29:40,612
‪how dare you not visit me once
‪while I was alive?"

388
00:29:40,695 --> 00:29:43,239
‪"You don't deserve a good night's sleep!"

389
00:29:43,323 --> 00:29:45,366
‪She was exactly how I remember her.

390
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:47,952
‪You know those old canes
‪that old people used?

391
00:29:48,036 --> 00:29:49,913
‪It hurt when she hit you, didn't it?

392
00:29:49,996 --> 00:29:51,790
‪Don't even ask. It hurt badly.

393
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:53,458
‪Who are you?

394
00:30:02,008 --> 00:30:03,718
‪That wasn't a dream.

395
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:05,595
‪Ms. Cheon?

396
00:30:08,932 --> 00:30:10,975
‪Cheon Yeo-ri.
‪It's Cheon Yeo-ri, the heiress.

397
00:30:11,059 --> 00:30:12,143
‪Mr. Ma.

398
00:30:13,645 --> 00:30:15,355
‪It's Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk.

399
00:30:15,438 --> 00:30:17,774
‪We shared a bed.

400
00:30:17,857 --> 00:30:19,359
‪You can't say that.

401
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:21,319
‪-People could get the wrong idea.
‪-What?

402
00:30:22,862 --> 00:30:24,697
‪What brings you here? Where are the rest?

403
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:27,867
‪I didn't bring anyone else.

404
00:30:27,951 --> 00:30:29,536
‪I'm here on my own.

405
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:31,913
‪I didn't think you'd step foot
‪in places like this.

406
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:34,123
‪They must know each other well.

407
00:30:34,207 --> 00:30:36,876
‪They don't just know each other.
‪I think they're best friends.

408
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:39,462
‪We can't stand not getting answers.

409
00:30:39,546 --> 00:30:40,797
‪-Right.
‪-Hello. How are you?

410
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:42,966
‪-Shall we?
‪-It's a pleasure to meet you.

411
00:30:43,466 --> 00:30:44,634
‪Stop.

412
00:30:46,928 --> 00:30:48,429
‪Maintain your distance.

413
00:30:49,222 --> 00:30:50,682
‪Take three steps back.

414
00:30:50,765 --> 00:30:52,433
‪Okay. Three steps back.

415
00:30:52,517 --> 00:30:54,143
‪One, two, three.

416
00:30:54,227 --> 00:30:55,562
‪-Sit down.
‪-Okay.

417
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:59,023
‪I'm doing this for your sake, you know.

418
00:30:59,107 --> 00:31:01,776
‪I'm putting up a wall to keep you safe.

419
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,820
‪If you make the mistake
‪of sitting with me,

420
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:06,322
‪terrible things could happen to you.

421
00:31:07,198 --> 00:31:10,076
‪That's why I paid in advance

422
00:31:11,119 --> 00:31:13,830
‪to keep the tables around me empty.

423
00:31:13,913 --> 00:31:17,292
‪So no one can even come near me.

424
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:19,377
‪I get that you want to flaunt your money,

425
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:21,588
‪but why bother to come here
‪just to drink alone?

426
00:31:22,547 --> 00:31:23,381
‪"Why bother"?

427
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:26,426
‪It's not the same.

428
00:31:26,509 --> 00:31:29,554
‪Here, if I look up from a drink,

429
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:30,930
‪I see people.

430
00:31:31,014 --> 00:31:33,641
‪At home, if I look up from a drink…

431
00:31:40,773 --> 00:31:41,608
‪Forget it.

432
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:45,403
‪-She emptied seven bottles of soju.
‪-She's out of it.

433
00:31:45,486 --> 00:31:48,406
‪Every now and then, I want to drink

434
00:31:48,489 --> 00:31:51,826
‪among some ordinary people.

435
00:32:02,545 --> 00:32:04,213
‪Wait…

436
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:05,965
‪Do it properly then.

437
00:32:06,049 --> 00:32:07,842
‪-What?
‪-Come and join us.

438
00:32:07,926 --> 00:32:09,802
‪-Yes, sure.
‪-Shall we?

439
00:32:09,886 --> 00:32:11,304
‪No, you can't.

440
00:32:12,138 --> 00:32:14,140
‪-Go away. Leave.
‪-Excuse us.

441
00:32:14,223 --> 00:32:18,019
‪If you join me,
‪you might get a taste of the afterlife.

442
00:32:18,102 --> 00:32:19,771
‪If we do, then so be it.

443
00:32:20,355 --> 00:32:21,189
‪Here.

444
00:32:22,690 --> 00:32:23,733
‪Drink up.

445
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:29,405
‪You filled my glass, so I should empty it.

446
00:32:33,409 --> 00:32:34,953
‪It's been so long

447
00:32:35,036 --> 00:32:37,497
‪since someone poured me a drink.

448
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:43,878
‪-They must have a thing.
‪-They're playing hard to get.

449
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:44,963
‪It's not like that.

450
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,006
‪It's not.

451
00:32:50,593 --> 00:32:53,680
‪Earlier, when I was talking about
‪the dream of my grandma,

452
00:32:53,763 --> 00:32:55,556
‪what did you mean it wasn't a dream?

453
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:57,517
‪Oh, that?

454
00:32:59,435 --> 00:33:00,812
‪You guys have no idea

455
00:33:01,562 --> 00:33:04,315
‪that the dead come visit you
‪while you sleep, do you?

456
00:33:05,900 --> 00:33:08,111
‪They come and watch you while you sleep.

457
00:33:09,195 --> 00:33:10,655
‪They just stare…

458
00:33:11,406 --> 00:33:12,240
‪like this.

459
00:33:12,824 --> 00:33:15,118
‪They sometimes give you sleep paralysis

460
00:33:15,868 --> 00:33:17,203
‪or even strangle you.

461
00:33:17,787 --> 00:33:20,790
‪People think they're just nightmares.

462
00:33:25,044 --> 00:33:26,546
‪You think they're all dreams, don't you?

463
00:33:31,175 --> 00:33:33,094
‪You would never know

464
00:33:33,177 --> 00:33:35,596
‪when you only ever see one side of things.

465
00:33:37,223 --> 00:33:39,100
‪You can't drink soju out of a bowl.

466
00:33:39,183 --> 00:33:40,351
‪That will kill you.

467
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:42,603
‪What? Why would I die?

468
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:46,441
‪No, I mean if you drink this much at once,

469
00:33:46,524 --> 00:33:48,192
‪it'll ruin your liver and your stomach.

470
00:33:48,276 --> 00:33:49,694
‪What if you were to fall ill?

471
00:33:49,777 --> 00:33:52,071
‪It'd be hard on you,
‪but also on your family.

472
00:33:52,155 --> 00:33:53,197
‪Shut up.

473
00:33:57,410 --> 00:34:00,371
‪You think my family would worry about me?

474
00:34:01,205 --> 00:34:02,040
‪What makes you say that?

475
00:34:03,249 --> 00:34:04,876
‪Do you even know me?

476
00:34:05,668 --> 00:34:08,588
‪What do you even know about me
‪to say something like that?

477
00:34:08,671 --> 00:34:11,924
‪What do people like you know

478
00:34:12,008 --> 00:34:14,385
‪when you're able to drink in a crowd?

479
00:34:14,469 --> 00:34:17,221
‪All you see with your two eyes
‪is the outer skin.

480
00:34:21,100 --> 00:34:21,934
‪Skin.

481
00:34:23,186 --> 00:34:24,520
‪This is a skin too.

482
00:34:25,396 --> 00:34:26,272
‪Skin.

483
00:34:29,817 --> 00:34:32,028
‪I don't need extra layers like these.

484
00:34:33,821 --> 00:34:36,741
‪Why'd you take off the gloves
‪you're always wearing?

485
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:47,752
‪-In this pork skin diner…
‪-What?

486
00:34:48,544 --> 00:34:50,296
‪Eating these pork skin…

487
00:34:52,090 --> 00:34:54,634
‪Only seeing the skin that meets the eye…

488
00:34:54,717 --> 00:34:57,845
‪-Wait…
‪-You're just a skin-deep prosecutor!

489
00:35:03,309 --> 00:35:05,520
<i>‪Skin-deep!</i>

490
00:35:06,104 --> 00:35:07,021
<i>‪What the…</i>

491
00:35:08,815 --> 00:35:11,359
<i>‪Skin-deep!</i>

492
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:22,120
<i>‪You should…</i>

493
00:35:24,580 --> 00:35:25,706
<i>‪be stripped…</i>

494
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:33,005
<i>‪of your skin!</i>

495
00:36:10,209 --> 00:36:11,085
‪Pil-dong.

496
00:36:12,545 --> 00:36:13,713
‪Can you lend me a shirt?

497
00:36:15,256 --> 00:36:16,924
‪I think you'll have to go home like that.

498
00:36:46,829 --> 00:36:48,122
‪What is this?

499
00:36:49,707 --> 00:36:52,793
<i>‪Man, never have I seen</i>
<i>‪such a drunken habit.</i>

500
00:36:52,877 --> 00:36:56,756
<i>‪I mean, forget that she was drunk,</i>
<i>‪but calling me "skin-deep"?</i>

501
00:36:56,839 --> 00:37:00,676
‪And why should I know her?
‪I could say the same about her.

502
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:04,597
‪Besides, why not drink on her own at home
‪instead of reserving half the diner?

503
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:07,016
‪She calls herself the CEO of a hotel,

504
00:37:07,099 --> 00:37:09,101
‪yet she pulls
‪a drunken stunt like that in public?

505
00:37:09,769 --> 00:37:12,313
‪Man, it was a new shirt too.

506
00:37:12,813 --> 00:37:15,900
‪Can't you at least react
‪at the bare minimum?

507
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:17,401
‪Hello?

508
00:37:19,028 --> 00:37:20,112
‪Did you say something?

509
00:37:21,697 --> 00:37:22,990
‪Oh, come on.

510
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:25,993
‪I'm sick of you. Get out.

511
00:37:26,702 --> 00:37:29,747
‪You can't corner me like this
‪just because we're carpooling in your car.

512
00:37:29,830 --> 00:37:32,375
‪I'm not cornering you.
‪We're here, so get out.

513
00:37:33,834 --> 00:37:35,336
‪Oh, when did we get here?

514
00:37:43,261 --> 00:37:45,096
‪Hello? You go ahead.

515
00:37:45,179 --> 00:37:47,431
<i>‪It's me, Cheon Yeo-ri.</i>

516
00:37:47,515 --> 00:37:48,599
‪What do you want?

517
00:37:49,433 --> 00:37:50,893
‪Well, I think…

518
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:54,105
‪I might have acted out of line last night.

519
00:37:54,188 --> 00:37:55,398
‪You mean ripping my shirt up?

520
00:37:56,565 --> 00:37:59,235
‪Don't worry about it.
‪It's fine. I threw it away.

521
00:37:59,735 --> 00:38:01,404
‪I'm not fine with what I did.

522
00:38:02,530 --> 00:38:05,199
‪I can't stand owing anyone anything.

523
00:38:06,867 --> 00:38:08,869
‪What did you send me?

524
00:38:15,710 --> 00:38:17,420
‪Yes, I knew it.

525
00:38:17,503 --> 00:38:18,838
‪It's Éthria.

526
00:38:21,173 --> 00:38:23,384
‪Look at this. It's pure silk.

527
00:38:23,467 --> 00:38:25,303
‪How much do these cost?

528
00:38:25,386 --> 00:38:27,722
‪This is a high-end luxury brand,

529
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:29,348
‪so at least three million won?

530
00:38:29,432 --> 00:38:30,641
‪What?

531
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:34,228
‪What's the nicest thing Ma can buy
‪without feeling guilty or tethered?

532
00:38:34,812 --> 00:38:35,855
‪Pork belly.

533
00:38:36,355 --> 00:38:37,815
‪What's the nicest thing he can accept?

534
00:38:38,649 --> 00:38:40,067
‪Two cups of iced coffee?

535
00:38:41,110 --> 00:38:43,821
‪That won't do. In that case,

536
00:38:43,904 --> 00:38:45,281
‪I'll carry it very safely…

537
00:38:45,364 --> 00:38:48,034
‪-Why would you take it?
‪-I should.

538
00:38:48,117 --> 00:38:50,453
‪Silk shirts look better on me.

539
00:38:50,536 --> 00:38:52,496
‪-You can't handle them.
‪-That's what you think.

540
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:53,998
‪You really can't handle a silk shirt.

541
00:38:54,081 --> 00:38:56,709
‪-You don't know--
‪-Éthria goods are…

542
00:38:56,792 --> 00:38:58,044
‪What? Mr. Ma.

543
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:01,088
‪That Éthria shirt…

544
00:39:13,934 --> 00:39:15,311
‪Hello, good morning.

545
00:39:15,394 --> 00:39:17,355
‪I'm here to see Ms. Cheon.

546
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:19,148
‪-Oh, Ms. Cheon?
‪-Yes.

547
00:39:19,231 --> 00:39:21,192
‪-Please give me a moment.
‪-Sure.

548
00:39:25,112 --> 00:39:26,489
‪-Hello.
‪-Yes, hi.

549
00:39:26,572 --> 00:39:28,824
‪The hotel gym and sauna, right?

550
00:39:31,952 --> 00:39:34,830
‪I'm Ms. Cheon's executive secretary.
‪Ms. Cheon isn't in at the moment.

551
00:39:37,083 --> 00:39:38,959
‪She sent this to me today.

552
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:40,753
‪If you're her secretary,
‪pass it to her for me.

553
00:39:40,836 --> 00:39:43,255
‪-No, I can't do that.
‪-Why not?

554
00:39:43,339 --> 00:39:44,715
‪If Ms. Cheon sent it to you herself,

555
00:39:44,799 --> 00:39:46,759
‪we're not allowed to
‪take it back on her behalf.

556
00:39:47,885 --> 00:39:50,388
‪What else am I supposed to do with it?

557
00:39:50,471 --> 00:39:53,015
‪Could you return it yourself,
‪if you don't mind?

558
00:39:55,518 --> 00:39:56,352
‪Jeez…

559
00:40:00,689 --> 00:40:01,524
‪Ms. Eom?

560
00:40:03,025 --> 00:40:06,779
‪Wasn't the man who came to see
‪Ms. Cheon here before?

561
00:40:06,862 --> 00:40:08,739
‪He was. This was his second visit.

562
00:40:09,782 --> 00:40:12,118
‪Could he be a stalker following Ms. Cheon?

563
00:40:12,201 --> 00:40:14,245
‪No, he's a Seoul
‪Central District prosecutor.

564
00:40:15,246 --> 00:40:17,331
‪Could he be pretending to be a prosecutor?

565
00:40:17,415 --> 00:40:18,290
‪I doubt that.

566
00:40:18,874 --> 00:40:22,628
‪His office once sent a questionnaire
‪to our legal team.

567
00:40:22,711 --> 00:40:24,338
‪Oh, right.

568
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:26,257
‪Do you know why
‪he wanted to see Ms. Cheon?

569
00:40:27,842 --> 00:40:30,219
‪It seems that Ms. Cheon sent him a gift

570
00:40:30,302 --> 00:40:31,595
‪and he wanted to return it.

571
00:40:32,638 --> 00:40:34,306
‪That's a problem.

572
00:40:34,974 --> 00:40:37,101
‪Whether it be from an official
‪or a private standpoint,

573
00:40:37,184 --> 00:40:40,688
‪it's a problem if she sent a gift
‪to a Central District prosecutor.

574
00:40:40,771 --> 00:40:44,108
‪Shouldn't we call a meeting
‪for damage control and countermeasures?

575
00:40:44,191 --> 00:40:47,945
‪If there is a problem,
‪I'm sure Ms. Cheon will handle it.

576
00:40:48,571 --> 00:40:49,488
‪No, no.

577
00:40:50,072 --> 00:40:52,825
‪We need to take action. My hunch says so.

578
00:40:53,492 --> 00:40:54,535
‪It's never wrong.

579
00:40:55,411 --> 00:40:56,495
‪Yes.

580
00:40:56,996 --> 00:40:58,080
‪That's my coffee.

581
00:40:58,622 --> 00:40:59,748
‪Oh, I was wrong.

582
00:41:01,709 --> 00:41:02,543
‪Wrong.

583
00:41:12,094 --> 00:41:15,890
‪It's not that big a favor.
‪Why couldn't she just return it for me?

584
00:41:15,973 --> 00:41:16,974
‪Jeez.

585
00:41:17,057 --> 00:41:18,684
‪Why does she live so far away?

586
00:41:33,240 --> 00:41:35,201
‪No wonder she reserved half the diner.

587
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:37,786
‪Where did they go?

588
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:39,955
‪They're the only thing that's missing.

589
00:41:41,373 --> 00:41:42,875
‪Where did I take them off?

590
00:41:46,879 --> 00:41:47,796
‪Who could that be?

591
00:41:48,422 --> 00:41:49,757
‪I didn't order any delivery.

592
00:41:56,472 --> 00:41:57,765
‪It's him again.

593
00:41:59,350 --> 00:42:00,476
‪What's he doing here?

594
00:42:04,230 --> 00:42:05,940
‪How did you find me?

595
00:42:06,023 --> 00:42:07,483
‪I put your address in my GPS.

596
00:42:08,526 --> 00:42:09,652
‪The GPS?

597
00:42:09,735 --> 00:42:12,029
‪How did you get my address?

598
00:42:13,239 --> 00:42:14,156
‪Don't you remember?

599
00:42:14,823 --> 00:42:15,866
<i>‪You gave it to me.</i>

600
00:42:15,950 --> 00:42:17,034
‪I did?

601
00:42:18,285 --> 00:42:19,328
‪I wouldn't…

602
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:38,806
‪Hey.

603
00:42:39,473 --> 00:42:41,517
‪Hello? Your address.

604
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:42,977
‪Tell me your address.

605
00:42:43,060 --> 00:42:43,978
‪My address?

606
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:48,232
‪-My address is Seongbuk-gu, Seoul…
‪-What?

607
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:51,652
‪Okay.

608
00:42:52,152 --> 00:42:53,946
‪Can you put this into the GPS?

609
00:42:58,867 --> 00:43:00,703
<i>‪I'm really sorry.</i>

610
00:43:00,786 --> 00:43:03,289
‪I was in the middle of something…

611
00:43:03,372 --> 00:43:04,290
<i>‪Never mind that.</i>

612
00:43:05,416 --> 00:43:07,042
‪I just came here to return this.

613
00:43:07,126 --> 00:43:09,545
‪I'm not able to come out right now.

614
00:43:10,296 --> 00:43:12,715
‪Could you leave it by the gate?

615
00:43:13,340 --> 00:43:14,717
‪Sure. I'll do that.

616
00:43:19,847 --> 00:43:21,765
<i>‪I'll leave these here as well.</i>

617
00:43:22,725 --> 00:43:24,059
<i>‪You left them at the diner.</i>

618
00:43:25,352 --> 00:43:26,186
‪What?

619
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:27,855
‪Why does he have my gloves?

620
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:38,157
‪I don't need extra layers like these.

621
00:43:40,451 --> 00:43:43,078
‪You should be stripped

622
00:43:43,162 --> 00:43:43,996
‪of your skin!

623
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:52,171
‪Hey, you forgot your gloves.

624
00:44:10,022 --> 00:44:10,856
‪Oh, no.

625
00:44:14,068 --> 00:44:15,569
‪I must've been out of my mind.

626
00:44:16,695 --> 00:44:18,697
<i>‪I'll leave both of these together</i>

627
00:44:18,781 --> 00:44:21,367
<i>‪-by the gate here.</i>
‪-I did that without my gloves?

628
00:44:23,869 --> 00:44:26,664
‪That's why I couldn't find them anywhere.

629
00:44:26,747 --> 00:44:28,624
‪-What now?
<i>‪-I've left them here.</i>

630
00:44:30,459 --> 00:44:31,293
‪I'm leaving now.

631
00:44:33,796 --> 00:44:34,880
‪Should I ask?

632
00:44:36,173 --> 00:44:37,966
<i>‪Wait. Wait.</i>

633
00:44:38,050 --> 00:44:38,884
‪What?

634
00:44:45,641 --> 00:44:48,018
‪What? Does she want me to come in?

635
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:19,716
‪Your house is really quiet.

636
00:45:21,135 --> 00:45:22,177
‪Yes.

637
00:45:25,722 --> 00:45:26,640
‪Look, Mr. Ma.

638
00:45:28,434 --> 00:45:31,103
‪By any chance, every now and then,

639
00:45:31,603 --> 00:45:34,731
‪do you happen to see things
‪you weren't able to before?

640
00:45:37,901 --> 00:45:40,237
‪There's a tent in your living room.

641
00:45:40,821 --> 00:45:42,489
‪Yes, well…

642
00:45:42,573 --> 00:45:45,033
‪It's pretty cozy inside.

643
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:48,912
‪As you can see,
‪this house is too big for me alone.

644
00:45:50,247 --> 00:45:51,582
‪It really is quite big.

645
00:45:51,665 --> 00:45:54,877
‪My parents used to live with me,
‪though not anymore.

646
00:45:57,921 --> 00:45:59,089
‪-Try the tea.
‪-Thanks.

647
00:46:07,931 --> 00:46:09,641
‪Why did you want me to come in?

648
00:46:09,725 --> 00:46:11,685
‪You don't seem the type to have guests.

649
00:46:12,728 --> 00:46:15,606
‪Well, you came all this way,

650
00:46:15,689 --> 00:46:18,233
‪so it felt wrong
‪to just send you on your way.

651
00:46:18,317 --> 00:46:20,068
‪And I wanted to check something too.

652
00:46:20,152 --> 00:46:22,196
‪Check what? With me?

653
00:46:23,155 --> 00:46:24,490
‪So last night…

654
00:46:25,282 --> 00:46:27,451
‪I was a bit out of line.

655
00:46:28,118 --> 00:46:30,746
‪I touched you without my gloves…

656
00:46:36,126 --> 00:46:37,294
‪Who's that kid?

657
00:46:45,594 --> 00:46:46,970
‪Who is that?

658
00:46:55,479 --> 00:46:57,940
‪-He's from next door.
‪-What's he doing here?

659
00:47:00,275 --> 00:47:01,318
‪Playing hide and seek.

660
00:47:01,401 --> 00:47:03,487
‪He comes here sometimes to play.

661
00:47:03,570 --> 00:47:05,197
‪Oh, really?

662
00:47:06,114 --> 00:47:07,241
‪He must be bored.

663
00:47:07,783 --> 00:47:09,743
‪If it's because his parents aren't home,

664
00:47:09,826 --> 00:47:11,495
‪-I'll play with him for a bit.
‪-No.

665
00:47:12,204 --> 00:47:13,205
‪You can't do that.

666
00:47:13,705 --> 00:47:14,748
‪You can't do anything.

667
00:47:14,831 --> 00:47:16,750
‪I'm really good with kids.

668
00:47:18,585 --> 00:47:21,004
‪You were here to return these, right?

669
00:47:21,088 --> 00:47:22,923
‪You returned them and I received them.

670
00:47:23,006 --> 00:47:24,049
‪All is well.

671
00:47:24,132 --> 00:47:26,176
‪You can leave now.

672
00:47:26,677 --> 00:47:27,719
‪Go on your way.

673
00:47:28,303 --> 00:47:29,137
‪Goodbye.

674
00:47:31,974 --> 00:47:33,642
‪-What was that?
‪-The wind.

675
00:47:35,477 --> 00:47:38,021
‪The doors are closed.
‪It couldn't have been the wind.

676
00:47:39,356 --> 00:47:41,358
‪Could it be a burglar?

677
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:42,734
‪What?

678
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:44,820
‪They could've scaled the wall
‪to hide somewhere.

679
00:47:44,903 --> 00:47:46,655
‪I worked on a case like that.

680
00:47:46,738 --> 00:47:49,283
‪Listen. I have a security system,

681
00:47:49,366 --> 00:47:50,867
‪so that would be impossible.

682
00:47:50,951 --> 00:47:51,785
‪Wait.

683
00:47:52,369 --> 00:47:53,704
‪I could just be paranoid,

684
00:47:53,787 --> 00:47:56,331
‪but it doesn't hurt to check,
‪and it won't take that long.

685
00:47:57,207 --> 00:47:58,041
‪No.

686
00:47:58,709 --> 00:47:59,668
‪It's not a burglar.

687
00:48:01,587 --> 00:48:03,630
‪It must've been the kid.

688
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:06,425
‪You see, there's an open door in the back.

689
00:48:06,508 --> 00:48:07,509
‪There is?

690
00:48:08,302 --> 00:48:10,095
‪Goodness, what a sneaky kid.

691
00:48:11,263 --> 00:48:12,389
‪Wait. Mr. Ma.

692
00:48:12,889 --> 00:48:14,266
‪It's fine. It won't take long.

693
00:48:14,349 --> 00:48:16,184
‪-I told you to go.
‪-Just wait.

694
00:48:17,561 --> 00:48:19,021
‪Are you in here?

695
00:48:19,104 --> 00:48:20,022
‪What?

696
00:48:20,105 --> 00:48:21,189
‪You're not in here.

697
00:48:21,857 --> 00:48:23,734
‪I'd better get going then.

698
00:48:23,817 --> 00:48:26,236
‪Ms. Cheon, you'll come with me, right?

699
00:48:26,987 --> 00:48:27,863
‪Where?

700
00:48:29,740 --> 00:48:31,658
‪-Come here.
‪-What are you…

701
00:48:32,367 --> 00:48:35,120
‪What are you doing?
‪How did you know this was a door?

702
00:48:35,203 --> 00:48:36,705
‪What are you…

703
00:48:51,553 --> 00:48:53,263
‪That must be him coming out.

704
00:48:54,556 --> 00:48:55,474
‪Who do you mean?

705
00:49:10,989 --> 00:49:12,616
‪Did you see that?

706
00:49:12,699 --> 00:49:13,909
‪He moved so fast.

707
00:49:13,992 --> 00:49:16,745
‪Gosh, it was like… He almost…

708
00:49:16,828 --> 00:49:17,663
‪That was…

709
00:49:18,163 --> 00:49:19,039
‪Excuse me.

710
00:49:19,122 --> 00:49:20,374
‪Yes?

711
00:49:20,957 --> 00:49:23,085
‪I'm really tired.

712
00:49:24,753 --> 00:49:25,587
‪Please leave.

713
00:49:27,673 --> 00:49:30,092
‪I was too dull-witted to catch on.

714
00:49:30,884 --> 00:49:31,927
‪I'm sorry.

715
00:49:43,021 --> 00:49:43,855
‪My coat.

716
00:49:52,489 --> 00:49:53,740
‪What should I do now?

717
00:49:54,991 --> 00:49:56,201
‪What do I do now?

718
00:50:18,265 --> 00:50:19,266
‪Will he be okay?

719
00:50:25,522 --> 00:50:26,815
‪What should I do?

720
00:50:56,720 --> 00:50:58,847
<i>‪What are you doing over there, kid?</i>

721
00:50:58,930 --> 00:51:00,640
<i>‪Shouldn't you be going home?</i>

722
00:51:01,475 --> 00:51:03,351
<i>‪Library hours are over now.</i>

723
00:51:06,062 --> 00:51:08,440
<i>‪I can't go home.</i>

724
00:51:30,378 --> 00:51:31,421
‪That hurt.

725
00:51:41,723 --> 00:51:42,557
‪I must be

726
00:51:43,517 --> 00:51:44,434
‪way too on edge.

727
00:52:12,838 --> 00:52:14,965
‪Why the hell won't this open?

728
00:52:20,637 --> 00:52:22,389
‪-Hello?
<i>‪-Hello?</i>

729
00:52:23,473 --> 00:52:24,724
‪He's in my home right now.

730
00:52:26,101 --> 00:52:28,353
‪-Who?
‪-The kid who was playing hide and seek.

731
00:52:32,190 --> 00:52:33,441
‪-The little boy?
<i>‪-Yes.</i>

732
00:52:33,525 --> 00:52:34,901
‪He came all the way to my home.

733
00:52:51,459 --> 00:52:52,460
‪Mr. Ma?

734
00:52:53,295 --> 00:52:54,129
‪I'm here.

735
00:52:54,629 --> 00:52:55,589
‪Over here.

736
00:52:58,717 --> 00:53:00,427
‪Were you out here this whole time?

737
00:53:04,347 --> 00:53:05,181
‪Sit down here with me.

738
00:53:06,391 --> 00:53:07,601
‪What…

739
00:53:09,060 --> 00:53:11,438
‪Who is that kid? He climbs walls too.

740
00:53:24,492 --> 00:53:26,286
‪SOJU

741
00:53:26,953 --> 00:53:28,455
‪You carry this stuff around with you?

742
00:53:28,538 --> 00:53:31,708
‪It's a bag I keep handy
‪in case of emergencies.

743
00:53:32,250 --> 00:53:33,627
‪Try to calm down.

744
00:53:34,836 --> 00:53:35,754
‪Drink that first.

745
00:53:49,434 --> 00:53:52,062
‪Do you feel a bit relaxed now?

746
00:53:53,813 --> 00:53:54,898
‪What do you mean "relaxed"?

747
00:53:54,981 --> 00:53:57,859
‪Are you going to say something
‪that'll shock me?

748
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:03,448
‪I have what it takes.
‪You can say whatever it is.

749
00:54:07,953 --> 00:54:08,954
‪Go on.

750
00:54:09,037 --> 00:54:09,955
‪Are you sure?

751
00:54:20,423 --> 00:54:21,341
‪No way.

752
00:54:40,110 --> 00:54:41,778
‪You weren't relaxed enough.

753
00:54:41,861 --> 00:54:44,489
‪Here. You need to stay with me.

754
00:54:45,031 --> 00:54:47,325
‪Have a few more sips of alcohol.

755
00:54:47,409 --> 00:54:49,244
‪Gulp it down. Don't spit it out.

756
00:54:56,001 --> 00:54:57,877
‪-He's not here.
‪-Okay.

757
00:55:01,006 --> 00:55:03,008
‪How did you know the body was there?

758
00:55:03,842 --> 00:55:05,343
‪-I was told.
‪-By whom?

759
00:55:06,678 --> 00:55:07,804
‪By a ghost.

760
00:55:09,139 --> 00:55:10,557
‪So she was telling the truth.

761
00:55:16,896 --> 00:55:18,064
‪Should I just turn the lights on?

762
00:55:18,982 --> 00:55:20,316
‪He doesn't like bright lights.

763
00:55:22,444 --> 00:55:23,903
‪You're sticking too close to me.

764
00:55:23,987 --> 00:55:25,905
‪I'm not standing that close.

765
00:55:25,989 --> 00:55:27,449
‪Wait outside if you're scared.

766
00:55:27,532 --> 00:55:30,243
‪I'm not scared, I'm just nervous.

767
00:55:34,039 --> 00:55:36,541
‪-Do you live alone too?
‪-Yes.

768
00:55:38,251 --> 00:55:41,504
‪Your place feels comfortable and cozy.

769
00:55:42,213 --> 00:55:45,925
‪I owe that to my grandma.
‪She sweeps and cleans whenever she visits.

770
00:55:46,426 --> 00:55:48,553
‪Huh? Wait…

771
00:55:50,972 --> 00:55:52,807
‪Does the kid like cars?

772
00:56:04,778 --> 00:56:06,446
‪He's a kid, so he'll be hiding.

773
00:56:10,075 --> 00:56:11,284
‪You must be good with housework.

774
00:56:11,868 --> 00:56:14,621
‪Yes. I'm good at everything I do.

775
00:56:36,935 --> 00:56:38,103
‪Oh, this is just…

776
00:56:38,937 --> 00:56:41,106
‪I always check out of habit.

777
00:56:41,189 --> 00:56:42,357
‪It's a work-related habit.

778
00:56:50,281 --> 00:56:52,117
‪Do you think he could've left?

779
00:56:54,536 --> 00:56:55,745
‪That's strange.

780
00:56:56,329 --> 00:56:58,915
‪Kids rarely leave
‪once they latch onto you.

781
00:57:00,416 --> 00:57:01,960
‪Where do they stay if they don't go?

782
00:57:04,879 --> 00:57:06,464
‪Why? What is it?

783
00:57:07,674 --> 00:57:08,883
‪Kids tend to…

784
00:57:08,967 --> 00:57:10,051
‪Yes?

785
00:57:12,470 --> 00:57:13,680
‪Piggyback on people.

786
00:57:28,528 --> 00:57:29,362
‪Get off me!

787
00:57:30,321 --> 00:57:32,574
‪-Mr. Ma! Keep still!
‪-Get off me!

788
00:57:32,657 --> 00:57:34,117
‪Go away!

789
00:57:35,285 --> 00:57:36,369
‪You said you weren't scared!

790
00:57:37,912 --> 00:57:40,039
‪No! No!

791
00:57:40,123 --> 00:57:41,207
‪Go away!

792
00:57:43,418 --> 00:57:45,170
‪He's off your back now!

793
00:57:45,253 --> 00:57:47,130
‪He's gone!

794
00:57:48,089 --> 00:57:49,549
‪He's gone!

795
00:57:50,049 --> 00:57:51,050
‪He's gone?

796
00:57:51,551 --> 00:57:52,469
‪He's gone?

797
00:58:45,855 --> 00:58:48,233
‪SPOOKY IN LOVE

798
00:58:48,316 --> 00:58:49,984
‪What do we do now?

799
00:58:50,068 --> 00:58:51,819
‪More ghosts will come for you.

800
00:58:53,780 --> 00:58:56,783
<i>‪What happened to the other people</i>
<i>‪you came in contact with?</i>

801
00:58:56,866 --> 00:58:59,118
<i>‪The ghosts that visit you early on</i>

802
00:58:59,202 --> 00:59:02,622
<i>‪will be the nasty ones</i>
<i>‪that harass and torment others.</i>

803
00:59:02,705 --> 00:59:03,957
<i>‪You believe in all this?</i>

804
00:59:04,040 --> 00:59:06,501
‪-There must be something about ghosts.
‪-Look.

805
00:59:06,584 --> 00:59:08,711
‪Look at him stuffing his face
‪with all that garlic.

806
00:59:08,795 --> 00:59:10,255
‪What's gotten into him?

807
00:59:10,338 --> 00:59:11,381
<i>‪You swore on your life</i>

808
00:59:11,464 --> 00:59:14,676
‪that you'd help me take over Reina
‪once you get out of here.

809
00:59:15,260 --> 00:59:16,094
‪Did you mean that?

810
00:59:17,053 --> 00:59:18,096
‪You bet I did.

811
00:59:18,930 --> 00:59:21,599
‪It makes no sense that a murderer like him
‪is getting released!

812
00:59:21,683 --> 00:59:23,101
‪Park Seung-jae.

813
00:59:23,184 --> 00:59:26,980
<i>‪I plan to find a weakness</i>
<i>‪instead of going after you,</i>

814
00:59:27,063 --> 00:59:28,064
<i>‪Cheon Yeo-ri.</i>

815
00:59:28,815 --> 00:59:33,820
‪Subtitle translation by: Jennifer Jean Lim
